1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:08,000
Simple Controller
A quick tour. One finger. Your way.

2
00:00:08,000 --> 00:00:13,000
Start in Practice. Nothing goes to Xbox.

3
00:00:13,000 --> 00:00:18,000
Touch. Drag. Explore.
Stop clears this phone’s actions.

4
00:00:18,000 --> 00:00:24,000
Stick+: move a little to walk.

5
00:00:24,000 --> 00:00:30,000
Move farther to add sprint.

6
00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:36,000
Reach the outer stage to add jump.
You choose the actions and distances.

7
00:00:36,000 --> 00:00:42,000
Need repeated presses?
Enable Repeat Stick+ buttons.

8
00:00:42,000 --> 00:00:50,000
Button Aim: touch and drag to aim.
One pad can aim and fire together.

9
00:00:50,000 --> 00:00:58,000
Choose its actions and sensitivity.
Act on touch or lift—no calibration needed.

10
00:00:58,000 --> 00:01:04,000
Drive + steer combines acceleration
with left-stick movement.

11
00:01:04,000 --> 00:01:10,000
Add up/down for flying.
Or separate steering, gas and brake.

12
00:01:10,000 --> 00:01:16,000
Hold to toggle: hold for its timer.
Lift: it stays on. Tap again: off.

13
00:01:16,000 --> 00:01:22,000
Double-tap to repeat keeps tapping.
Tap once to stop.

14
00:01:22,000 --> 00:01:28,000
More choices: Auto-Tap repeats after one tap.
Turbo repeats while you touch.

15
00:01:28,000 --> 00:01:34,000
Auto-center off keeps a stick moving.
Center stops sticks. Stop clears all phone actions.

16
00:01:34,000 --> 00:01:39,000
A small directional pad can send
all four D-pad directions.

17
00:01:39,000 --> 00:01:44,000
Hold the wheel; drag to choose.
Check your game’s mapping.

18
00:01:44,000 --> 00:01:48,000
Enable sliding to move between
ordinary buttons without lifting.

19
00:01:48,000 --> 00:01:54,000
Floating controls appear near your touch.
Rings use distance to add actions.

20
00:01:54,000 --> 00:02:00,000
Aim, hold or repeat from the ring.
Finish closes it. No contact calibration.

21
00:02:00,000 --> 00:02:06,000
TouchAim uses finger-contact size
to choose Aim or Shoot stages.

22
00:02:06,000 --> 00:02:12,000
Open Touch inspector first.
Contact size is not pressure.

23
00:02:12,000 --> 00:02:18,000
Comfortable touches look the same?
Choose Button Aim or a ring instead.

24
00:02:18,000 --> 00:02:23,000
Macro Mode finishes after you lift.
Choose actions, delays and press lengths.

25
00:02:23,000 --> 00:02:28,000
Each press releases automatically.
Stop cancels the sequence.

26
00:02:28,000 --> 00:02:34,000
Tap Edit, then drag a control.
Use the edges, too.

27
00:02:34,000 --> 00:02:40,000
Hold to change its size or actions.
Tap Done, then Save to keep changes.

28
00:02:40,000 --> 00:02:45,000
Hide a menu. Drag its little circle.
Tap to open it again.

29
00:02:45,000 --> 00:02:50,000
Move actions with the arrow.
Choose Vertical toolbar in ….

30
00:02:50,000 --> 00:02:56,000
Profiles hold your controllers.
Pages keep their controls organized.

31
00:02:56,000 --> 00:03:02,000
Choose a Game starter.
Its Menus page keeps navigation nearby.

32
00:03:02,000 --> 00:03:09,000
Mouse, keys and Camera Follow:
use the free PC receiver.

33
00:03:09,000 --> 00:03:16,000
Copy profiles. Reuse settings.
Export a backup. Import or recover it later.

34
00:03:16,000 --> 00:03:21,000
Connect to a PC or console.
Support shows the setup steps.

35
00:03:21,000 --> 00:03:26,000
USB buttons means full press or release.
Adjustable pressure needs matching hardware.

36
00:03:26,000 --> 00:03:30,000
Start small. Find your rhythm.
Make it yours.
